    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for the E.164 telephone on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**What the spec required:** reject with 400 when the national-number length is wrong for the country code \u2014 `+61` needs 9 national digits, `+1` needs 10.\n\n**Changes** (all in the create-owner telephone pipeline):\n\n1. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 added a `NATIONAL_LENGTHS` map (`\"61\"\u21929`, `\"1\"\u219210`) and a new `hasValidNationalLength(String e164)` helper. It isolates the country code from the E.164 digits (longest known prefix wins, so `+61` isn't mistaken for `+1`) and checks the remaining national digits against the required count. Unknown country codes fall back to the existing generic 8\u201315 rule. I kept `toE164` as pure normalization so the idempotent comparison in `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique` is unaffected.\n\n2. **`NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`** \u2014 the validating step now throws `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` (\u2192 400) when either normalization fails *or* the national length is wrong for the country.\n\n3. Updated the javadoc on `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` and `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` to document the new rejection reason.\n\n**Why this is the right seam:** `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` is the pipeline's telephone-validating step, and it already routes `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` through the existing `officefloor/escalation/...InvalidOwnerTelephoneException.yml` \u2192 `InvalidOwnerTelephoneExceptionHandler`, which returns `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"telephone\"]}`. No new YAML or handler was needed.\n\n**Verification:** `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` (posts `\"+61 123\"`, expects 400) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). Note that the existing valid-owner payload (`uniqueTelephone()` \u2192 `04XXXXXXXX` \u2192 `+61` + 9 national digits) still satisfies the new rule, so happy-path creates continue to succeed.",
